  "content": {
    "id": "p42-q6",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Let $p(x)=x(x-2)$ and $d(x)=2x$. When $p(x)$ is composed with $d(x)$ the result is a transformation since $d(x)$ is linear.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p42-q6-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Write down the domain and range of $y=p(x)$. A sketch may help.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Domain: $x\\in\\mathbb R$. Range: $y\\geq-1$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}p(x)&=x^2-2x\\\\p(x)&=(x-1)^2-1\\end{align*}$$\nThe minimum output is $-1$, attained at $x=1$.\n\nDomain: $x\\in\\mathbb R$. Range: $y\\geq-1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p42-q6-b",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the values of:",
        "layout": "grid",
        "columns": 2,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p42-q6-b-i",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "i",
            "prompt": "$p(d(1))$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$0$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}d(1)&=2\\\\p(d(1))&=p(2)\\\\p(d(1))&=2(2-2)=0\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 18
          },
          {
            "id": "p42-q6-b-ii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "ii",
            "prompt": "$d(p(1))$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$-2$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}p(1)&=1(1-2)=-1\\\\d(p(1))&=d(-1)\\\\d(p(1))&=2(-1)=-2\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 18
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p42-q6-c",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Find expressions for:",
        "layout": "grid",
        "columns": 2,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p42-q6-c-i",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "i",
            "prompt": "$p(d(x))$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$p(d(x))=4x(x-1)$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}p(d(x))&=p(2x)\\\\p(d(x))&=2x(2x-2)\\\\p(d(x))&=4x(x-1)\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 18
          },
          {
            "id": "p42-q6-c-ii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "ii",
            "prompt": "$d(p(x))$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$d(p(x))=2x(x-2)$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}d(p(x))&=2p(x)\\\\d(p(x))&=2x(x-2)\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 13
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p42-q6-d",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p42-q6-d-i",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "i",
            "prompt": "What transformation maps the graph of $y=p(x)$ to the graph of $y=p(d(x))$?",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "Horizontal stretch with factor $\\tfrac12$.",
              "worked": "$p(d(x))=p(2x)$. Each point $(x,y)$ on $y=p(x)$ maps to $(\\tfrac{x}{2},y)$, so the transformation is a horizontal stretch with factor $\\tfrac12$.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 22
          },
          {
            "id": "p42-q6-d-ii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "ii",
            "prompt": "Hence write down the domain and range of $y=p(d(x))$.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "Domain: $x\\in\\mathbb R$. Range: $y\\geq-1$.",
              "worked": "The horizontal stretch leaves the domain as all real numbers and preserves the minimum output $-1$.\n\nDomain: $x\\in\\mathbb R$. Range: $y\\geq-1$.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 10
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p42-q6-e",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p42-q6-e-i",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "i",
            "prompt": "What transformation maps the graph of $y=p(x)$ to the graph of $y=d(p(x))$?",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "Vertical stretch with factor $2$.",
              "worked": "$d(p(x))=2p(x)$, so each output is multiplied by 2. This is a vertical stretch with factor 2.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 10
          },
          {
            "id": "p42-q6-e-ii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "ii",
            "prompt": "Hence write down the domain and range of $y=d(p(x))$.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "Domain: $x\\in\\mathbb R$. Range: $y\\geq-2$.",
              "worked": "The vertical stretch preserves the domain and multiplies the minimum output $-1$ by 2.\n\nDomain: $x\\in\\mathbb R$. Range: $y\\geq-2$.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
